{
  "deviations_and_caveats": [
    "The full `MCPROOF_LIVE_LLAMA_TESTS=1 pytest stack/tests/test_stack_suite.py` end-to-end live test (Phase 4 + full Phase 6 T-C1..T-C5) was NOT run. It needs lab-host prerequisites that the UX582HS host doesn't have (siliconcordat `mde` Rust binary, `exo`, `warp_modeld`, `weft` sibling repos, and the LlamaServerClient they provide); its lab tests self-skip. T-C5 was replayed instead with a standalone harness that reproduces the exact T-C5 server flags, prompt, sampling and interleaving. phase6_receipt.json and docs/CONTINUITY.md in the repo were not modified (no push).",
    "llama.cpp build is b12549 (version string 1.0.0-dev); the issue requires >= 0.5.0. The M1 Max reference used llama-server 0.5.0, so absolute tok/s are not comparable across hosts.",
    "Measured peak VRAM is well above the analytical baselines in the issue (Q8_0 4.9451 headless / 6.1451 WDDM GiB; Q4_K_M 3.4034 / 4.6034 GiB). Main cause: hardware_probe.compute_rtx3080_vram_fit and the phase6 projection count F16 KV for ONE 8192-token sequence (0.25 GiB), but the T-C5 server config (-np 8, -c 65536, kv_unified=false) allocates KV for 8 x 8192 tokens (about 2.0 GiB), plus 8 recurrent-state copies and the CUDA context. The analytical +1.20 GiB WDDM desktop allowance did not materialize (the dGPU drives no display). Q8_0 headroom under the 7.2 GiB gate is 0.35 GiB.",
    "8-slot overhead is an extra measurement (the issue checklist mentions single-slot / 8-slot). The original harness only measures single-slot on the np8 instance. Both are gated here.",
    "KV residency stress filled each slot to 7486/8192 tokens (91.4%), not the full 8192; KV is preallocated at boot, so VRAM did not change materially (+10 MiB) under load.",
    "A preliminary Q8_0 run (runs/q8_0_prelim.json, before the content-hash LoRA check was added) gave matching numbers: peak 7017 MiB, single-slot overhead -0.22%, 8-slot -1.01%."
  ],
